cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BreedingR: genetic parameters, breeding values and genomic prediction in R"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Freitas
    given-names: Felipe Andre Oliveira
    affiliation: "Escola Superior de Agricultura Luiz de Queiroz (ESALQ), Universidade de Sao Paulo, Brazil; Purdue University, West Lafayette, IN, USA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/phyllype/BreedingR"
abstract: >-
  An R package for variance components by AI-REML, breeding values, accuracy and
  single-step genomics, with reaction norms, direct-maternal and indirect genetic
  effect models, AR(1)/CAR(1) residuals, a Gibbs sampler, APY and Vecchia inverses,
  markers as equations, metafounders, quality control and selection-signature scans.
  The numerics live in the package itself, in C++, with no run-time dependency.
  Developed during doctoral research at the Escola Superior de Agricultura Luiz de
  Queiroz (ESALQ), Universidade de Sao Paulo, and at Purdue University, with support
  from the Sao Paulo Research Foundation (FAPESP), grants 2024/15502-6 and
  2025/02949-5 (BEPE); the
  Coordenacao de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nivel Superior (CAPES), Finance Code
  001; and the Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Cientifico e Tecnologico (CNPq).
keywords:
  - animal breeding
  - quantitative genetics
  - AI-REML
  - single-step genomic prediction
  - reaction norm
  - indirect genetic effects
version: 0.4.0
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/phyllype/BreedingR/blob/main/LICENSE"
